WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:03.334
-Our next guest has her
comedy album "Logging Out"

00:00:03.334 --> 00:00:05.334
available now on Apple Music.

00:00:05.334 --> 00:00:06.701
Making her "Tonight Show" debut,

00:00:06.701 --> 00:00:09.367
please welcome
the very funny Samantha Ruddy.

00:00:09.367 --> 00:00:12.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:12.534 --> 00:00:17.767
♪♪

00:00:17.767 --> 00:00:20.267
-Thank you!

00:00:20.267 --> 00:00:22.534
Ah. It's great to be here.

00:00:22.534 --> 00:00:25.334
I flew on a tiny plane,
like three years ago,

00:00:25.334 --> 00:00:28.033
and every day since
has just been a nice bonus.

00:00:28.033 --> 00:00:29.734
[ Laughter ]

00:00:29.734 --> 00:00:32.467
It was so small,
they had to take our weights.

00:00:32.467 --> 00:00:35.300
My girlfriend called me.
She was like, "Sam,

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:37.000
I need to know
how much you weigh."

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:40.334
I was like,
"Oh, um, 160 pounds?"

00:00:40.334 --> 00:00:42.667
She was like,
"I need your real weight."

00:00:42.667 --> 00:00:44.434
[ Laughter ]

00:00:44.434 --> 00:00:46.567
"'Cause it's
to balance the plane out."

00:00:46.567 --> 00:00:50.434
I was like, "Oh, sorry.
Uh, 180 pounds?"

00:00:50.434 --> 00:00:53.434
She was like,
"The plane will crash."

00:00:53.434 --> 00:00:55.000
[ Laughter ]

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:57.801
"We will not get to see
my family this weekend."

00:00:57.801 --> 00:01:00.834
I was like, "Oh, I'm so sorry.
I didn't know

00:01:00.834 --> 00:01:03.167
that we wouldn't have to
hang out with your family."

00:01:03.167 --> 00:01:05.367
[ Laughter ]

00:01:05.367 --> 00:01:07.133
"I weigh 50 pounds."

00:01:07.133 --> 00:01:09.167
[ Laughter ]

00:01:09.167 --> 00:01:14.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:14.534 --> 00:01:16.834
I don't even like
flying on regular planes.

00:01:16.834 --> 00:01:18.501
Too risky.

00:01:18.501 --> 00:01:21.767
The most dangerous thing
that I do is I cut my own hair.

00:01:21.767 --> 00:01:25.901
And I only do that because I got
the worst haircut of my life

00:01:25.901 --> 00:01:28.534
from a salon.
It was so bad

00:01:28.534 --> 00:01:30.634
that before the woman
was even finished,

00:01:30.634 --> 00:01:32.567
she said, "Ah, it'll grow back."

00:01:32.567 --> 00:01:34.734
[ Laughter ]

00:01:34.734 --> 00:01:37.901
She gave me, like, swoopy bangs
in the front

00:01:37.901 --> 00:01:40.167
and then spiky on top.

00:01:40.167 --> 00:01:42.400
She gave me the Karen.

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:44.834
[ Laughter ]

00:01:44.834 --> 00:01:46.968
And you know
what the worst part was?

00:01:46.968 --> 00:01:49.334
I couldn't even complain.

00:01:49.334 --> 00:01:52.734
[ Laughter ]

00:01:52.734 --> 00:01:56.300
[ Applause ]

00:01:56.300 --> 00:01:58.968
Because that's exactly
what a Karen would do.

00:01:58.968 --> 00:02:00.601
[ Laughter ]

00:02:00.601 --> 00:02:02.400
She'd be like, "Do you
want to talk to the manager?

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:03.934
Because you look like you do."

00:02:03.934 --> 00:02:05.300
[ Laughter ]

00:02:05.300 --> 00:02:07.400
One nice thing
about cutting my own hair is

00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:10.067
it saves money.
I am horrible with money,

00:02:10.067 --> 00:02:12.300
and I can pinpoint
the exact moment

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:14.033
where things went wrong.

00:02:14.033 --> 00:02:15.634
My senior year of high school.

00:02:15.634 --> 00:02:17.400
We got to pick electives.

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:21.701
I chose to take philosophy
instead of money management.

00:02:21.701 --> 00:02:23.033
[ Laughter ]

00:02:23.033 --> 00:02:26.334
And to this day, I cannot
balance a checkbook.

00:02:26.334 --> 00:02:28.868
But I do know

00:02:28.868 --> 00:02:31.334
nothing about philosophy,
either.

00:02:31.334 --> 00:02:32.767
[ Laughter ]

00:02:32.767 --> 00:02:36.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:36.868 --> 00:02:39.100
People are like, "Why is
your credit score so low?"

00:02:39.100 --> 00:02:41.634
And I'm like, "Can one truly
score your credit?"

00:02:41.634 --> 00:02:43.400
[ Laughter ]

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:45.167
They can.

00:02:45.167 --> 00:02:48.467
540.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:48.467 --> 00:02:50.467
Another reason I think
I'm bad with money is

00:02:50.467 --> 00:02:52.734
'cause my mom never let me
do anything for myself.

00:02:52.734 --> 00:02:54.400
She still doesn't.

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:56.033
I was shopping
with her recently.

00:02:56.033 --> 00:02:57.934
I wanted to buy
a violent video game.

00:02:57.934 --> 00:02:59.467
She cut me off.

00:02:59.467 --> 00:03:01.367
On my way to the cashier,

00:03:01.367 --> 00:03:03.901
she was like,
"Hey, Mr. GameStop,

00:03:03.901 --> 00:03:06.901
I just have to ask,
is this game violent?"

00:03:06.901 --> 00:03:08.934
And he was like, "Yeah."

00:03:08.934 --> 00:03:11.634
And my mom said, "Well,
I'm just worried

00:03:11.634 --> 00:03:13.467
about my kid playing it."

00:03:13.467 --> 00:03:15.634
And he goes, "Well,
how old is your kid?"

00:03:15.634 --> 00:03:18.567
And my mom says, "29."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:18.567 --> 00:03:20.634
And then, I swear to God,
he just looked at me

00:03:20.634 --> 00:03:23.334
and he was like,
"Is it this woman?"

00:03:23.334 --> 00:03:25.133
[ Laughter ]

00:03:25.133 --> 00:03:28.133
I was like, "You heard the lady.
Can I handle it or not?"

00:03:28.133 --> 00:03:30.300
[ Laughter ]
I couldn't.

00:03:30.300 --> 00:03:32.701
[ Laughter ]
It's really violent.

00:03:32.701 --> 00:03:35.000
I have nightmares every night.

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:38.434
Don't play "Madden."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:38.434 --> 00:03:40.901
Thanks.
[ Applause ]

00:03:40.901 --> 00:03:44.501
Thank you. Thanks.

00:03:44.501 --> 00:03:46.901
I love football,
but I've been trying

00:03:46.901 --> 00:03:49.634
to get into the NBA
because it's way gentler.

00:03:49.634 --> 00:03:52.000
You know, even
the team names in the NBA

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:54.767
are less aggressive
than NFL team names.

00:03:54.767 --> 00:03:57.334
The NFL is like, "We're
the Minnesota Vikings.

00:03:57.334 --> 00:03:58.934
We're fierce."

00:03:58.934 --> 00:04:02.067
The NBA is like,
"We're the Utah Jazz."

00:04:02.067 --> 00:04:06.467
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:06.467 --> 00:04:08.734
"We're difficult to appreciate."

00:04:08.734 --> 00:04:10.467
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:10.467 --> 00:04:13.234
"We're the Denver nuggets.

00:04:13.234 --> 00:04:15.067
We're four for a dollar."

00:04:15.067 --> 00:04:16.367
[ Laughter ]

00:04:16.367 --> 00:04:18.434
I didn't have any choice
but to like sports.

00:04:18.434 --> 00:04:20.367
I grew up with three brothers.

00:04:20.367 --> 00:04:22.634
We like to argue over
who my mom's favorite is.

00:04:22.634 --> 00:04:24.701
But even more than that,
we like to argue

00:04:24.701 --> 00:04:27.067
over who her least favorite is.

00:04:27.067 --> 00:04:28.801
I thought I was gonna get her
the other day.

00:04:28.801 --> 00:04:30.567
I was like, "Mom,
you're trapped in a room

00:04:30.567 --> 00:04:32.868
with the four of us
and a killer.

00:04:32.868 --> 00:04:35.501
One of us has to go.
Who do you pick?"

00:04:35.501 --> 00:04:39.467
And she was like, "Well,
I guess I would pick me."

00:04:39.467 --> 00:04:41.033
"Ohh."

00:04:41.033 --> 00:04:42.834
And then she said,
"Because I have no interest

00:04:42.834 --> 00:04:45.100
in being trapped in a room
with even three of you."

00:04:45.100 --> 00:04:47.067
[ Laughter ]

00:04:47.067 --> 00:04:49.501
She has
a vicious sense of humor.

00:04:49.501 --> 00:04:52.701
One time, my brother
called me an ignoramus.

00:04:52.701 --> 00:04:55.534
And she said, "Hey, you can't
talk to her like that.

00:04:55.534 --> 00:04:57.834
You have to use smaller words."

00:04:57.834 --> 00:04:59.901
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:59.901 --> 00:05:02.133
Alright, thank you so much.
I really appreciate it.

00:05:02.133 --> 00:05:04.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:04.767 --> 00:05:07.067
-Hey! Come on, pal!

00:05:07.067 --> 00:05:09.767
Samantha Ruddy!

00:05:09.767 --> 00:05:12.133
"Logging out" is available
on Apple Music.

00:05:12.133 --> 00:05:14.133
We'll be right back,
ladies and gentlemen.

